    <string name="help_auto_dc_title">Auto and data center addresses</string>
    <string name="help_auto_dc_text">With Cloudflare on, you usually don\'t need manual DC addresses: the proxy takes the CF route. With Cloudflare off, the connection goes straight to Telegram DCs and you can set addresses by hand. DC2 and DC4 are usually enough; the rest are for manual setup and diagnostics.</string>
    <string name="help_cloudflare_text">This mode sends the connection through WebSocket domains behind Cloudflare. It is more stable on some mobile networks, but the result depends on the route, DNS and provider. If connecting got slower, compare with CF off.</string>
    <string name="help_ws_pool_text">The number of WebSocket connections prepared in advance. A larger pool can cut the delay on first connect and media loading, but adds background connections. 2–4 is usually enough. Raise it only if you see a benefit on your network.</string>
    <string name="help_secret_key_text">The 16-byte MTProto encryption key. Change it only if the connection link reached someone else.</string>
    <string name="help_experimental_text">Opens manual setup for all regular and media data centers: DC1, DC3, DC5, DC203 and their media variants. It is for diagnostics, tests and unusual routes. Keep it off unless you need that.</string>
    <string name="help_autostart_text">The proxy tries to start by itself after the device reboots. On some firmware this takes a while: the system may wait for Android to finish booting or for the first unlock.</string>
    <string name="help_slow_connect_title">If connecting takes long</string>
    <string name="help_slow_connect_text">If Telegram hangs on connecting after the proxy starts, the current route is probably bad and the app itself is fine. Restart the proxy and compare with Cloudflare on and off.</string>
    <string name="understood">Got it</string>
    <string name="hero_description">Local MTProto proxy on the Flowseal core, with a direct route and Cloudflare mode. It runs on the device; no root or VPN needed.</string>
